{"id":"f1eab1108defb738","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-equivalence-formula.md","title":"Equivalence Formula","display":"df-equivalence-formula — Equivalence Formula","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-equivalence-formula","aliases":["93-df-equivalence-formula"],"display":"df-equivalence-formula — Equivalence Formula","depends_on":["[[93-df-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-equivalence-formula"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-equivalence-formula</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-equivalence-formula — Equivalence Formula"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c2ca1af9af149e69\" href=\"?note=c2ca1af9af149e69\" title=\"93-df-formula\">93-df-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\">\\(\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\\)</span> is a connective-type candidate, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\to,\\land\\in S\">\\(\\to,\\land\\in S\\)</span> are candidate binary symbols.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\">\\(\\mathrm{SimilarityType}\\)</span> is the arity-signature predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\">\\(\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\\)</span> is the indexed formula carrier of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c2ca1af9af149e69\" href=\"?note=c2ca1af9af149e69\" title=\"93-df-formula\">93-df-formula</a>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(-,-;\\to,\\land)\">\\(\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(-,-;\\to,\\land)\\)</span> is defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\\coloneqq\n\\land\\bigl(\\to(\\varphi,\\psi),\\to(\\psi,\\varphi)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\\coloneqq\n\\land\\bigl(\\to(\\varphi,\\psi),\\to(\\psi,\\varphi)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\to,\\land\\in S\n\\land\\alpha(\\to)=2\n\\land\\alpha(\\land)=2\n\\land\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\\Bigr]\\to\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\n\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\to,\\land\\in S\n\\land\\alpha(\\to)=2\n\\land\\alpha(\\land)=2\n\\land\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\\Bigr]\\to\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\n\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Prefix constructor notation makes this a formula code in the term algebra; it is not a meta-level conjunction of two assertions. Both connective maps and the formula signature are explicit, so the constructor cannot change meaning with ambient notation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"c2ca1af9af149e69","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-similarity-type","status":"resolved","id":"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SimilarityType}$ is the arity-signature predicate of [[93-df-similarity-type]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"c2ca1af9af149e69","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)$ is the indexed formula carrier of [[93-df-formula]], and $\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(-,-;\\to,\\land)$ is defined here.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\to,\\land\\in S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SimilarityType}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(-,-;\\to,\\land)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\\coloneqq\n\\land\\bigl(\\to(\\varphi,\\psi),\\to(\\psi,\\varphi)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}equivalence\\text{-}formula}\\vdash\n\\Bigl[\\tau=\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{SimilarityType}(S,\\alpha)\n\\land\\to,\\land\\in S\n\\land\\alpha(\\to)=2\n\\land\\alpha(\\land)=2\n\\land\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)\\Bigr]\\to\n\\mathrm{EquivForm}_{93}(\\varphi,\\psi;\\to,\\land)\n\\in\\operatorname{Fm}_{93}(\\tau)","display":true}],"bytes":1444,"backlinks":[{"id":"173103b981643051","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"57abb955e28f83aa","anchor":"ref-72","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[93-df-equivalence-formula]]"}],"outgoing":["c2ca1af9af149e69","ee84ed8b0fae5bc3"]}